.TH dumpbt "1" "" "The scalpel3 Block Type Dumper" "The scalpel3 Block Type Dumper"

.SH NAME
dumpbt \- Display a scalpel3 block classification database

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dumpbt
[block_classification_database_pathname]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBdumpbt\fR validates and displays the contents of a
\fIblockclassification.dat\fR file written by \fBscalpel3\fR after block
validation.  It reports the database dimensions and file type mapping, then
prints each file type's per-block confidence values.  Consecutive blocks with
the same confidence are combined into ranges for readability.
.PP
Block numbers start at zero and refer to positions in the evidence image,
not positions in a compacted view. Confidence values range from 0 (invalid)
through 100 (valid). Consult the associated blockmap for duplicate/exemplar
relationships and coverage; a confidence value is not a coverage flag.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.PP
.TP
.I [block_classification_database_pathname]
Optional. The path to the block classification database. If not specified, it
defaults to "scalpel-output/blockclassification.dat".

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero for a successfully read database and nonzero for an unreadable,
unsupported, or malformed database.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scalpel3 (1),
.BR dumphf (1)

.SH AUTHOR
Golden G. Richard III.
